{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WxyiBGxGoS7R3NfAWzd3hJ","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"EMNLP 2025 review form scoring rubric acceptance rate\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"EMNLP 2025 Statistics - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/emnlp-statistics/emnlp-2025-statistics/\"},{\"title\":\"Conference Decisions · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://gist.github.com/antonisa/2158dee79179c7c49304ef353887bfa0\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP Statistics - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/emnlp-statistics/\"},{\"title\":\"FAQ - EMNLP 2025\",\"url\":\"https://2025.emnlp.org/faq/\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP 2025 Decisions: Community Insights and the Controversial Desk Rejections | CSPaper Forum\",\"url\":\"https://forum.cspaper.org/topic/131/emnlp-2025-decisions-community-insights-and-the-controversial-desk-rejections\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP 2025 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=EMNLP%2F2025%2FConference\"},{\"title\":\"[EMNLP 2025] First Call for Papers | ACL Member Portal\",\"url\":\"https://www.aclweb.org/portal/content/emnlp-2025-first-call-papers\"},{\"title\":\"Review Form\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP 2025 Industry Track | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=EMNLP%2F2025%2FIndustry_Track\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP 2024 Statistics - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/emnlp-statistics/emnlp-2024-statistics/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found regarding EMNLP 2025:\n\n## Acceptance Rate\n\nEMNLP 2025 had a Main acceptance rate of just over 22%.\n\n## Review Form Scoring\n\nFor the review form, EMNLP 2025 uses the ARR (ACL Rolling Review) system. The scoring rubric includes: 3 = Acceptable: This study provides sufficient support for its main claims with some minor points that may need extra support or details; 2 = Poor: Some of the main claims are not sufficiently supported. Additionally, there is a score for \"Consider for Award\" for papers that could be considered for outstanding paper awards (up to top 2.5% papers).\n\n## Key Decision Metrics\n\nAccording to community analysis of the EMNLP 2025 decisions, meta-review scores of ≥ 3.5 often lead to Main acceptance, scores of 3 are unstable (leading to Findings, Rejection, or occasionally Main), and scores < 3 almost always mean rejection with rare exceptions.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"93355213-87f8-4b5a-b04b-1b0ebb649ece","uuid":"c42c9784-1f2e-45dc-8f57-20063c2c2813","timestamp":"2026-05-16T17:32:40.566Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"EMNLP 2025 review form scoring rubric acceptance rate","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_014ts6W51nhfr4yNDNSeWG4z","content":[{"title":"EMNLP 2025 Statistics - Paper Copilot","url":"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/emnlp-statistics/emnlp-2025-statistics/"},{"title":"Conference Decisions · GitHub","url":"https://gist.github.com/antonisa/2158dee79179c7c49304ef353887bfa0"},{"title":"EMNLP Statistics - Paper Copilot","url":"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/emnlp-statistics/"},{"title":"FAQ - EMNLP 2025","url":"https://2025.emnlp.org/faq/"},{"title":"EMNLP 2025 Decisions: Community Insights and the Controversial Desk Rejections | CSPaper Forum","url":"https://forum.cspaper.org/topic/131/emnlp-2025-decisions-community-insights-and-the-controversial-desk-rejections"},{"title":"EMNLP 2025 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=EMNLP%2F2025%2FConference"},{"title":"[EMNLP 2025] First Call for Papers | ACL Member Portal","url":"https://www.aclweb.org/portal/content/emnlp-2025-first-call-papers"},{"title":"Review Form","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform"},{"title":"EMNLP 2025 Industry Track | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=EMNLP%2F2025%2FIndustry_Track"},{"title":"EMNLP 2024 Statistics - Paper Copilot","url":"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/emnlp-statistics/emnlp-2024-statistics/"}]},"Based on the search results, here's what I found regarding EMNLP 2025:\n\n## Acceptance Rate\n\nEMNLP 2025 had a Main acceptance rate of just over 22%.\n\n## Review Form Scoring\n\nFor the review form, EMNLP 2025 uses the ARR (ACL Rolling Review) system. The scoring rubric includes: 3 = Acceptable: This study provides sufficient support for its main claims with some minor points that may need extra support or details; 2 = Poor: Some of the main claims are not sufficiently supported. Additionally, there is a score for \"Consider for Award\" for papers that could be considered for outstanding paper awards (up to top 2.5% papers).\n\n## Key Decision Metrics\n\nAccording to community analysis of the EMNLP 2025 decisions, meta-review scores of ≥ 3.5 often lead to Main acceptance, scores of 3 are unstable (leading to Findings, Rejection, or occasionally Main), and scores < 3 almost always mean rejection with rare exceptions."],"durationSeconds":6.153756965999997}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014dibNd5TRucNqUwnJz3b5e","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"EMNLP 2026 reviewer guidelines review form\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"FAQ - EMNLP 2026\",\"url\":\"https://2026.emnlp.org/faq/\"},{\"title\":\"LINGUIST List 37.972 Confs: 2026 Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing (Hungary)\",\"url\":\"https://linguistlist.org/issues/37/972/\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP 2026 : The 2026 Conference on Empirical Methods in N\",\"url\":\"https://callforpaper.org/call-for-papers-emnlp-2026\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP 2026 | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=EMNLP%2F2026\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=EMNLP\"},{\"title\":\"Authors Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/authors\"},{\"title\":\"Changes to reviewer volunteering requirement and incentives in May 2025 cycle (EMNLP 2025)\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/incentives2025\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP 2025 (@emnlpmeeting) · X\",\"url\":\"https://twitter.com/emnlpmeeting\"},{\"title\":\"CALL FOR PAPERS – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/cfp\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP 2026 (@emnlpmeeting) / Posts / X\",\"url\":\"https://x.com/emnlpmeeting\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about EMNLP 2026 reviewer guidelines and review forms:\n\nEMNLP 2026 uses the Open Review platform for submissions and commitment. Authors submit articles to ACL Rolling Review (ARR), where submissions receive reviews and meta-reviews from ARR reviewers and action editors, then commit their reviewed articles to EMNLP 2026, where Senior Area Chairs and Program Chairs make acceptance decisions from the ARR reviews and meta-reviews.\n\nAll reviewers must familiarize themselves with the latest version of the ARR reviewer guidelines and perform the reviews on time and in line with ARR requirements.\n\nRegarding key deadlines for EMNLP 2026 reviewers: If you receive assignments, your reviews must be completed by July 6, or your meta-reviews - by July 29.\n\nThe search results reference the ARR reviewer guidelines but don't provide the specific review form details directly. For the complete reviewer guidelines and review form template, you would need to visit the ACL Rolling Review website directly (aclrollingreview.org) or the EMNLP 2026 official website (2026.emnlp.org), where the specific review form fields and guidelines are maintained.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"93355213-87f8-4b5a-b04b-1b0ebb649ece","uuid":"bc1c1176-65a9-4633-80eb-7d6ad0132743","timestamp":"2026-05-16T17:32:42.443Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"EMNLP 2026 reviewer guidelines review form","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_019pT6znokjC4chADnjpkwvX","content":[{"title":"FAQ - EMNLP 2026","url":"https://2026.emnlp.org/faq/"},{"title":"LINGUIST List 37.972 Confs: 2026 Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing (Hungary)","url":"https://linguistlist.org/issues/37/972/"},{"title":"EMNLP 2026 : The 2026 Conference on Empirical Methods in N","url":"https://callforpaper.org/call-for-papers-emnlp-2026"},{"title":"EMNLP 2026 | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=EMNLP%2F2026"},{"title":"EMNLP | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=EMNLP"},{"title":"Authors Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/authors"},{"title":"Changes to reviewer volunteering requirement and incentives in May 2025 cycle (EMNLP 2025)","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/incentives2025"},{"title":"EMNLP 2025 (@emnlpmeeting) · X","url":"https://twitter.com/emnlpmeeting"},{"title":"CALL FOR PAPERS – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/cfp"},{"title":"EMNLP 2026 (@emnlpmeeting) / Posts / X","url":"https://x.com/emnlpmeeting"}]},"Based on the search results, here's what I found about EMNLP 2026 reviewer guidelines and review forms:\n\nEMNLP 2026 uses the Open Review platform for submissions and commitment. Authors submit articles to ACL Rolling Review (ARR), where submissions receive reviews and meta-reviews from ARR reviewers and action editors, then commit their reviewed articles to EMNLP 2026, where Senior Area Chairs and Program Chairs make acceptance decisions from the ARR reviews and meta-reviews.\n\nAll reviewers must familiarize themselves with the latest version of the ARR reviewer guidelines and perform the reviews on time and in line with ARR requirements.\n\nRegarding key deadlines for EMNLP 2026 reviewers: If you receive assignments, your reviews must be completed by July 6, or your meta-reviews - by July 29.\n\nThe search results reference the ARR reviewer guidelines but don't provide the specific review form details directly. For the complete reviewer guidelines and review form template, you would need to visit the ACL Rolling Review website directly (aclrollingreview.org) or the EMNLP 2026 official website (2026.emnlp.org), where the specific review form fields and guidelines are maintained."],"durationSeconds":8.312694615999996}}
