{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01HTbzodUpWskmpEgn2Vjm1h","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Lwe9c8VKc2fkXMotvhqgLJ","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"R1: Methods + Experiments review","prompt":"You are Reviewer 1 (R1) for an EMNLP 2026 submission. Your focus areas are **Methods** and **Experiments**. \n\n## Venue: EMNLP 2026 (via ACL Rolling Review)\n- Overall assessment scale: 1–5 (5=Excellent, 4=Strong, 3=Acceptable, 2=Poor, 1=Major Issues)\n- Three dimensions: Soundness, Excitement, Overall Recommendation\n- Acceptance rate: ~22%\n\n## Paper Summary\n**Title**: \"Phase-Stratified Diagnosis of Compound Sparsity Interactions: The Interaction Index Framework\"\n\nThe paper introduces the Interaction Index (II), a per-problem paired diagnostic metric with bootstrap CIs and phase-stratified decomposition, for diagnosing compound sparsity (attention head pruning + KV cache eviction) interactions in LLMs. Key claims:\n\n1. **II metric** (Eq 1): per-problem paired difference between compound degradation and sum of individual degradations, with phase stratification (Eq 2) into low-sparsity (0-33% tokens) and high-sparsity (67-100% tokens) phases.\n2. **Phase gradient universality**: within-importance dz > 0.95 across 3 architectures (DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B, Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct, DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Llama-8B), all CIs exclude zero.\n3. **Strategy specificity is context-dependent**: importance/random ratio 15–36× on MATH-500, 2.3–3.8× on GSM8K, 1.1–1.3× on GPQA-Diamond; absent on LLaMA (dz < 0.20).\n4. **Discrimination collapse**: within-model Gini–II Spearman ρ=1.0 (trivially, n=4 monotonic points), cross-model Pearson r=0.48 (NS, p=0.115).\n5. **Language switching** (§4.5): monotonic dose-response in DeepSeek, acknowledged as bilingual-model-specific.\n\n## Experimental Design Reference (from review_context.yaml)\nThe imagined experiments include:\n- **LLaMA n=250**: Confirms imp_vs_rand dz all <0.20, zero Bonferroni-significant. Random phase gradient persists (dz 0.30-0.38). Strategy specificity architecture-dependent.\n- **GPQA DeepSeek profiling**: Gradient monotonic but magnitude ~10% of MATH-500 (s030: 0.855 vs 8.48). s015 CI crosses zero (p=0.085).\n- **GPQA Qwen profiling**: Even weaker (s030: 0.52). Mid-null rate 55%, effective n=89.\n- **GPQA random baselines**: Strategy specificity ratio 1.1-1.3× (effectively absent). Decay: MATH 15-36× → GSM 2.3-3.8× → GPQA 1.1-1.3×.\n- **Gini-II correlation**: Within-model ρ=1.0 trivial (4 monotonic points). Cross-model r=0.48 NS. No LLaMA Gini data.\n- **Language switching**: Actual data complete, monotonic. But reviewer concern: DeepSeek bilingual artifact.\n\n## Your Task (R1: Methods + Experiments)\n\nProduce a detailed review covering:\n\n### 1. Summary (2-3 sentences)\n### 2. Strengths (bullet points)\nFocus on methodological soundness, statistical framework, experimental design.\n\n### 3. Weaknesses (bullet points)\nFocus on:\n- Statistical concerns (n=4 trivial correlations, cross-model r=0.48 NS, Bonferroni failures)\n- Phase stratification is a simple 33/67 percentile split — is this well-motivated?\n- II metric is literally just the interaction term from a 2×2 factorial — how novel is this methodologically?\n- Only 7B-scale models tested\n- GPQA results: s015 CI crosses zero, high mid-null rates, effective n drops substantially\n- LLaMA validation reveals original claims were inflated by small-sample noise (n=50 pilot)\n- No computational overhead analysis of the audit protocol\n- Missing reference formatting (\"??\" in citations)\n\n### 4. Questions for Authors\n### 5. Scores\n- Soundness (1-5)\n- Excitement (1-5)  \n- Overall Assessment (1-5)\n- Confidence (1-5)\n\nBe rigorous. This is a top venue with ~22% acceptance rate. The paper needs to clear a high bar for methodological contribution and experimental rigor."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2300,"cache_read_input_tokens":54322,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2300},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"93355213-87f8-4b5a-b04b-1b0ebb649ece","uuid":"78d04026-abd8-405b-8639-143433063c1d"}
