{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018jxahnXiSiUbusRxukbcb3","type":"tool_result","content":"artifacts/_project/paper/analysis.tex:4:[Omitted long matching line]\nartifacts/_project/paper/analysis.tex:9:[Omitted long matching line]\nartifacts/_project/paper/conclusion.tex:4:[Omitted long matching line]\nartifacts/_project/paper/limitations.tex:17:Importance discrimination collapse is a correlational diagnostic observation, not a causal explanation: both strategies exhibit near-identical Gini drops yet severity diverges by $15$--$17{\\times}$, indicating that Gini collapse alone is insufficient. Causal validation through controlled entropy manipulation is needed. The entropy redistribution component replicates on only 2/4 Qwen conditions, suggesting model-specific factors.\nartifacts/_project/paper/response_letter.md:16:- **N2**: Section 6 restructured --- discrimination collapse framed as correlational diagnostic (not mechanism); structural specificity introduced as key differentiator; per-sparsity matched imp/rand Delta-Gini comparison added; entropy redistribution trimmed to supplementary observation (~50 words)\nartifacts/_project/paper/abstract.tex:7:Per-phase Gini analysis identifies \\emph{importance discrimination collapse}---the degeneration of head importance scores toward uniformity under compound stress---as a correlational diagnostic of this severity divergence.\nartifacts/_project/paper/introduction.tex:19:Per-phase Gini analysis identifies \\emph{importance discrimination collapse}---the degeneration of head importance scores toward uniformity under compound stress---as a correlational diagnostic of this phase--strategy divergence. Both strategies exhibit consistent Gini drops across all tested conditions, yet severity diverges by $2.7$--$17{\\times}$, implicating the structural specificity of importance-based pruning as the key differentiator.\nartifacts/_project/paper/introduction.tex:27:    \\item We identify \\textbf{importance discrimination collapse} via per-phase Gini analysis as a correlational diagnostic: consistent collapse across models and strategies, with the structural specificity of importance-based pruning corresponding to the severity divergence (\\S\\ref{sec:analysis})."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01Lwe9c8VKc2fkXMotvhqgLJ","session_id":"93355213-87f8-4b5a-b04b-1b0ebb649ece","uuid":"692afaf4-1ac1-40c1-81c0-3f2c5fb6533f","timestamp":"2026-05-16T17:34:25.276Z"}
